-- title:
--   Power series expansion of the pole chart ring at ∞
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field and let $A$ be an integrally closed integral domain equipped with an $L$-algebra-compatible structure making $L$ its fraction field, so that $A \subseteq L$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field between $L$ and the field $L((q))$ of formal Laurent series over $L$, carrying an $A$-algebra structure compatible with that of $L$ via the scalar tower $A \to L \to K$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero and assume that the Laurent series of $j^{-1}$ has vanishing coefficient in degree $n$ for every $n \le 0$. Write $B =$ `chartAlgInf` $A\,K\,j$ for the subalgebra of $K$ consisting of the elements integral over the $A$-subalgebra $A[j^{-1}]$ of $K$ generated by $j^{-1}$. Then there are ring homomorphisms $\iota : B \to L[[q]]$ and $\chi : B \to A$ such that: the Laurent series underlying $\iota(b)$ is the Laurent series of $b$ for every $b \in B$; the image of $\chi(b)$ in $L$ is the constant coefficient of $\iota(b)$ for every $b \in B$; $\iota$ sends the image of $a \in A$ in $B$ to the constant power series with value the image of $a$ in $L$; and $\iota$ carries the element $j^{-1}$ of $B$ to $q \cdot \sum_{n \ge 0} c_{n+1} q^{n}$, where $c_m$ denotes the degree-$m$ coefficient of the Laurent series of $j^{-1}$.
--
--   This is the algebraic core of the $q$-expansion principle at the cusp $\infty$: elements of the pole chart ring of the two-chart integral model are power series in $q$ with constant term in the ring of constants $A$, together with the explicit expansion of $j^{-1}$. It supplies the chart datum used in the analysis of the minimal primes of the ideal generated by $j^{-1}$ on the full-level modular curve.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel_exists_ringHom_powerSeries_chartAlgInf_coe_eq_and_algebraMap_eq_coeff_zero.lean

import Mathlib
